35
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:36,228
Zero commercial activity allowed, which was fine, until people showed up on the internet who wanted to be customers.

36
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:39,588
And a few businesses, eight to be exact, showed up who wanted to serve them.

37
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:45,796
If a customer of one wanted to email a customer of the other, the only wire between them was the one they weren't allowed to use.

38
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:49,956
So the two companies had to physically touch their wires together somewhere.

39
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:54,560
A line coming out of one building, a line coming out of the other, and physically meeting somewhere.

40
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,640
That was the only way two customers could talk.

41
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,172
It's kind of crazy to think about how they solved it.

42
00:02:59,502 --> 00:03:09,508
Just a couple of guys, one from each of these first companies, ran a wire from the street, one for each company, and into the first meeting place, which was just a plain office suite in a building in Tyson's Corner, Virginia.

43
00:03:09,902 --> 00:03:11,920
Two companies at first, then another and another.

44
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:17,200
Within two months, eight offices were connected together, each company running a line from their building and into this room.

45
00:03:17,454 --> 00:03:21,700
Once more companies joined in that room filled with cables, they moved across the street to a parking garage.

46
00:03:21,998 --> 00:03:25,572
Actually, a tiny room off the garage of an office building on Boone Boulevard.

47
00:03:25,838 --> 00:03:27,120
One server, one plug.

48
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:27,600
That was it.

49
00:03:27,726 --> 00:03:29,412
Nobody worked there, nothing was computed there.

50
00:03:29,614 --> 00:03:32,420
It was a place for a handful of companies to touch their wires together.

51
00:03:33,006 --> 00:03:35,332
Yes, I said it again, and I'll probably say it a fourth time.

52
00:03:35,886 --> 00:03:38,884
This was the first public internet and the world's first data center.

53
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:43,108
A room whose whole point was simply a meeting place for other buildings around it to touch.

54
00:03:43,502 --> 00:03:53,680
By the time the government shut off the wire companies weren't allowed to use, around half the world's internet traffic was already passing through that little room in that garage in Tyson's Corner, Virginia.

